<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 17 August, from 1424 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1424">1424 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">602 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English army defeats a Franco-Scottish force at Verneuil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Duke of Bedford's army won a bloody victory over French and Scottish troops at Verneuil in Normandy. Hailed as a second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a>, it secured English control of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> for years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Fulton's steamboat begins its voyage up the Hudson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Robert Fulton's North River Steamboat left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> and reached Albany in 32 hours of running. It launched the first commercially successful steamboat service, transforming river travel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bridget Driscoll becomes Britain's first pedestrian killed by a car</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bridget Driscoll was struck by a demonstration car in the grounds of the Crystal Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. The coroner hoped such a thing would never happen again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sukarno proclaims Indonesian independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s surrender, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-hatta">Mohammad Hatta</a> proclaimed independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fought to return, but transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in 1949.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1988">1988 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pakistan's President Zia ul-Haq dies in a plane crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-zia-ul-haq">Muhammad Zia-ul-Haq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>'s military ruler for eleven years, died when his C-130 crashed near Bahawalpur. The US ambassador also died; the cause has never been established.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
